   "subject": "Re: [methylkit_discussion] memory usage",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Jamal,<div>How many CpGs  and samples you have in your  methylBase object &quot;meth&quot; ? That would affect the memory usage and since you are doing it on two cores, your R session might be duplicating everything in your session so it will increase the memory if you use multiple cores. </div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>You can try to save your &quot;meth&quot; object and start a fresh R session and redo the calculation, this way intermediate objects will be removed from memory and hopefully it won&#39;t take as much memory as before.</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Oct 9, 2013 at 2:22 PM, Jamal Momeni <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Jamal....@agrsci.dk</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
